# Reservation Lifecycle

OfficeFlow reservations use exactly four statuses in `ReservationStatus`:

`Pending` → `Confirmed` → `Completed`  
          ↘ `Cancelled` (from Pending or Confirmed only)

## Allowed transitions

| From | To | How |
| --- | --- | --- |
| — | `Pending` | Create reservation |
| `Pending` | `Confirmed` | Manager `Confirm()` / `POST …/confirm` |
| `Pending` or `Confirmed` | `Cancelled` | Manager or owning Tenant `Cancel()` / `POST …/cancel` |
| `Confirmed` | `Completed` | `TryCompleteIfDue` when `Period.EndUtc <= now` (background job) |

## Rules

- **Do not add** statuses like `Rejected`, `Paid`, `Expired` to `ReservationStatus`.
- Payment (if introduced later) is a **separate** concept (`PaymentStatus` / payment entity), not a reservation status.
- Domain methods live on `Reservation`: `Confirm()`, `Cancel()`, `Complete()`, `TryCompleteIfDue(utcNow)`.
- Auto-complete only for **Confirmed** past end; never invent other auto-transitions.
- Recalculate cost only while `Pending` or `Confirmed`.
- API: Manager confirms; cancel allowed for Manager or owning Tenant (claims) — see `auth-and-roles.mdc`.
- Frontend: expose Confirm/Cancel only for valid statuses; do not invent extra status chips.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
reservation.Confirm();
reservation.TryCompleteIfDue(clockUtc);

// ❌ BAD — new enum value or illegal jump
Status = ReservationStatus.Rejected;
reservation.Complete(); // while still Pending
```
